!! Vitals

* ''Branch'' `feature/lararium-node-5`, ahead of `origin` — `git rev-list --count origin/feature/lararium-node-5..HEAD` reads the unpushed commits; the operator pushes. Crew-held dirt in the tree: `mempalace` and `VSCode-TW5-Syntax` (submodule pointers), `tests/harness/instance.ts`, untracked `tests/e2e/nexus-offering-replication.test.ts`, `bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/`, `.worktrees/`, `.claude/worktrees/`. Never commit, stash, or revert those.
* ''Landed in the last sign-off'' (CHANGELOG `[Unreleased]`, the SIGN-OFF BATCH lines): the first arrival — the descriptor at `/.well-known/lar` (`application/vnd.lar.arrival+json`, mirrors from `LAR_PRONAOS_MIRRORS`), `kindle.ts#pullArrival`, a waking-floor lararium serving all of it; anchored ancestry — a seal roll lands a roll anchor (domain `carriage-roll-anchor`) and an admit in its causal past carries to the head; the quoteblock floor's whole-chunk grain (`ingest-gate.ts` `wholeChunkFloor`) beside the child grain; parallel drafts persisted to the reading wiki's draft bag (`wikis/<slug>/draft`) through a `ParallelDraftsReader`; submissions titled `submissions/<name>` with `--title-base` removed; the face-grant record carrying no wall clock; the tree-sitter CLI and runtime pinned at 0.27.0.
* ''E2E'' (the whole staged set): 27 of 29 files, 205 tests passed. The two reds: the crew's untracked `tests/e2e/nexus-offering-replication.test.ts`, and a race in `tests/e2e/corpus-feed.test.ts` F2 — its walker meets a disk projector's `*.lar-tmp-*` file (`disk-projector.ts`) that is renamed away before the read (ENOENT); it passes 4 of 4 alone (`#/wounds` 6).
* ''The witness fleet'' (`tools/witness-all.sh`, what CI runs) ends on a verdict table, one line per witness with its own exit code — count the reds there, never in the transcript. 31 of 32 read ok; `vessel-parity-witness` reads red (`makePersonaGroupIdentityRing` composes on node only — the browser side is owed). `contract-witness` reads ok through ⑩, anchored ancestry. Each dist-reading witness refuses a stale build by name (exit 2) — rebuild the named package, run `node tools/stamp-build.mjs . --pkg <name>`, re-run; a comment edit in a package's `src/` stales its dist too.
* ''Typecheck'' (`tools/typecheck-witness.sh`): every package clean across 11 projects.
* ''Unit suites'': `lararium-tw5` 1696 of 1703 (6 skipped, 1 red: `tests/carrier-edges.test.ts` reads 174 dangling edges against a ceiling of 172 — the +2 stand in the offering-antigen crew's `bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/offering-antigen-scope-local-b.mem:201-204`, theirs to settle); `lararium-mesh` 2414 passed; `lararium-node` 1356 passed and 1 expected fail.
* ''CI'' (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`): the last run read a pushed head behind the local tree — `gh run list --branch feature/lararium-node-5` names it. The next push is the witness for everything since.
* ''The tree is shared'': a parallel lane edits `bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/wsl2/**` and `tools/wsl2/**` and re-stamps after editing — a witness run mid-edit reads its carriers as drifted for a minute. Re-run before believing a red there.
* ''Known test reds'' and their owners:
** `lararium-tw5` `tests/carrier-edges.test.ts` — the offering-antigen crew (above).
** `lararium-sensorium` `scripts/test_structure_router.py::test_ahu_block_nests_inner_sigils` reads one inner sigil where it asserts two — red on the desk and in CI.
