<<~ ahu #/wounds>>

!! Open wounds — round 4, ranked

The sign-off reviewed the last four lanes and found no blocker; what it found stands here in the order to take it.

# ''MED — a raise presents without roll anchors.'' `packages/lararium-node/src/commands/raise-sign.ts:105` builds its presented admit off the board's entries without the board's roll anchors, so an admit at a rolled epoch presents with no chain to the head. Collapse the four callers onto ONE board-doc presenter helper, and add a post-roll raise test.
# ''MED — the syncer ingest door drops the floor's warnings.'' `packages/lararium-tw5/src/action-handler.ts:895` discards `placed.warnings`, so a `quoteblocked` finding on that door reaches no one. Carry the warnings through and pin it with a test.
# ''MED — two doors skip the whole-chunk floor.'' The LOAD door (`action-handler.ts:732`) and the registered deserializer (`packages/lararium-tw5/src/deserializer.ts:608`) read a carrier without `wholeChunkFloor`. Either gate them, or re-true `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/ahu` `:132-133` and `:140`, which claim every door — a ruling for the hand that takes it; this sign-off re-trued neither.
# ''MED — the rotate's ordering is untested at its own level.'' A rotate-level test: an anchor refusal leaves the charter unwritten, and the anchor lands before `writeNexusSeal`.
# ''LOW — an orphan anchor on a same-commit retry.'' A rotate retried over the same commit can leave an anchor that no charter head follows, and the presenter chooses among anchors by CID order.
# ''LOW — the corpus-feed walker races the projector's temp files.'' Tolerate ENOENT, or skip `*.lar-tmp-*`, in the F2 walker (`tests/e2e/corpus-feed.test.ts`). Hand the `carrier-edges` +2 to the offering-antigen crew.
# ''LOW — the Pronaos reads its house origins from a lararium alone.'' `packages/lararium-node/src/main.ts:198` hands the mirror check an empty `houseOrigins` when the standing is not `lararium`. `kindle.ts#pullArrival` is library-only — no verb reaches it — against `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/pronaos` `:225`; wire a door or re-true the carrier (a ruling, as in 3).
# ''LOW — draft persistence fires and forgets.'' The island adaptor's `ParallelDraftsReader` write reports a failure through `console.warn` alone, and a null destination skips in silence; route both to the alert rail.
# ''LOW — a wall clock still signs inside the face-grant record.'' The `DeviceDelegation` `founderEdge` carried in the record still signs `issuedAt`/`expiresAt`.

